    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        40,
        400
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "How to use\n\n1. Pick your checkpoint in Load Checkpoint.\n2. While exploring prompts, select the hires-pass nodes (ImageScaleBy through Save Image) and press Ctrl+B to bypass them. You then only get the fast base preview.\n3. When you like an image, set the base KSampler seed to fixed, un-bypass the hires nodes (Ctrl+B again) and run once more.\n\nHires pass: denoise 0.35 to 0.45 adds detail. Higher values start changing the picture.\nIf the hires pass runs out of memory, lower scale_by to 1.3 or start ComfyUI with --lowvram.\n\nAnime Post FX: set any effect to 0 to turn it off.\n\nStyle reference (purple group): the IPAdapter copies lighting, color and rendering from the three reference images, not their characters. Default is 0.45 with style transfer precise. Above about 0.6 the image turns flat and oversaturated. The result follows the references' color palette, so pick references whose lighting mood you want. Swap images in the Style reference nodes (click the image, or drag a new one onto the node). To turn it off, select the IPAdapter node and press Ctrl+B."
      ]
    },
